jailgrid is a console for FreeBSD jails on several hosts, published as
geass.  A progressive web app, logged in to with a security key
(WebAuthn), shows every jail of every host, starts, stops and restarts
them, and changes their addresses live, in jail.conf, or both, with a
diff to preview first.  Every action comes with its workflow as a graph:
the library calls, system calls and programs it used, and the programs'
raw output.

Each jail host runs jailgridd(8), which manages its jails with libjail,
libprocstat and jail(8), and serves them over cblink with mutual TLS.
The console is a Kore module, unprivileged.  jailconf(8) changes one
value in jail.conf in place, like sysrc(8) does for rc.conf, and
jailgridctl(8) talks to a jailgridd from a shell.

Without the CONSOLE option only the jail host's programs are built.
